  <h2 id="changes">Every confirmed change</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Area</th><th>What changes in 1.0</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Spells</td><td>9 new spells: Mana Drain, Entangle, Pillar of Flames, Blizzard, Ball Lightning, Summon Fire/Ice/Shock Totem and Summon Hollow Skeleton. Spells gain more versions, including 22 tier-7 Eternal versions that skip ammo and can be upgraded.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Wands</td><td>Piercing heavy attacks that interrupt weaker enemies, plus Aerial and Evasion attacks, improved targeting and explosive-barrel targeting.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Archery</td><td>Three new Eternal arrows (Fire, Shock, Bone); all Eternal arrows are now upgradeable. New skills: Puncture, Barrage, Survival Instinct.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Skills</td><td>8 new skills and a full skill tree reset — re-spend your points.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>New biome</td><td>Cinder's Cradle opens the northern edge of Embervale: a lava-scarred wasteland beneath floating islands raised by the Ancients, with Shroud tendrils between them. It adds 12 Shroud Roots, while newly accessible outskirts in other biomes add 6 more. Two new Hollow Halls open in the Albaneve Summits and the Veilwater Basin.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Story</td><td>The current Embervale story reaches its conclusion. Main quests return players to earlier regions, including structures that were previously inaccessible. The Shroud and the Fell remain as threats.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Progression</td><td>Player level cap 50, equipment level 55, and a new crafting tier covering gear, tools, food, arrows, spells and base-building items. A new survivor focused on Ancient knowledge and recipes joins your settlement.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Enemies</td><td>Cinder's Cradle introduces a new faction with 14 enemy types. Including additions to existing factions, 1.0 brings 37 new enemy types and variants, some of them heavy or elite.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Building</td><td>Sparkworks: a logic system wiring levers, pressure plates and triggers to doors, trapdoors, traps, lightning, released water and enemy spawns. Builders also get a free-flying build mode, and storage chests can be upgraded without emptying them first.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Adventure Sharing</td><td>Supports player-made dungeons and mini-games; browse Popular Adventures, filter by tags, use Share Codes, subscribe to favourites.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Balance</td><td>Mana costs and cast times re-tuned against spell damage and usability; enemy elemental weaknesses reworked.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Updraft</td><td>A setting lets you choose the original instant version or the newer version with a charge time.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Character</td><td>New character proportions as an appearance option; existing characters can update their look through Elio Ricci.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Fishing</td><td>Bait primarily attracts fish from the biome its resources came from; better bait matches fish tier. Fishing location no longer determines the base catch chance, though spots still favour more bites or more treasure/trash.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>NPCs and pets</td><td>Fixes for inhabitants getting stuck around player-built bases.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Voice acting</td><td>Lore notes, letters and books are voiced in English, German and Mandarin Chinese, with playback controls that let you queue entries into a playlist. Main crafting survivors and major quest-givers are voiced in those languages too.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Visuals</td><td>A new brick-rendering method shows more detail in distant terrain and voxel buildings, including player-built structures. Biomes get distinct lighting, atmosphere and moisture settings, and HDR is supported on compatible displays.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Early game</td><td>New chests plus revised roads and camps make early exploration more rewarding and easier to follow, and crafting recipes were adjusted to cut down on resource grinding.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Performance</td><td>Rendering, lighting, shadows and distant scenery were reworked alongside reduced memory use, with attention to lower- and mid-range PCs.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="biome">Cinder's Cradle: the new 1.0 biome</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p>
      Cinder's Cradle opens the northern edge of Embervale, the region players could previously only see
      from a distance. It contains two contrasting areas: a <strong>lava-scarred wasteland</strong> on
      the ground and <strong>floating islands raised by the Ancients</strong> above it, with Shroud
      tendrils stretching between them. It is the largest single content addition in 1.0, and the reason
      both the level and gear caps rise.
    </p>
    <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
      <li><strong>12 Shroud Roots</strong> in Cinder's Cradle itself, plus <strong>6 more</strong> in newly accessible outskirts of other biomes.</li>
      <li><strong>Two new Hollow Halls</strong> — one in the Albaneve Summits, one in the Veilwater Basin.</li>
      <li><strong>A new faction</strong> with 14 enemy types, part of the 37 new enemy types and variants in 1.0.</li>
      <li><strong>Story finale</strong> — main quests return you to earlier regions, including previously inaccessible structures.</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0;margin-top:0.75rem">
      Practical implication: the new caps (level 50, gear 55) exist because Cinder's Cradle is tuned
      above the old endgame. Do not go straight there. Re-spend your skill points, upgrade your gear, and
      enter with a build that handles groups — the new faction fields more enemies than anything in the
      base game.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="saves">Saves, price and Early Access owners</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
      <li><strong>Your save is safe.</strong> Early Access saves remain usable in 1.0; they convert to the updated save format when you move to the full release.</li>
      <li><strong>Restarting is optional.</strong> You are not forced into a new character.</li>
      <li><strong>No re-purchase on PC.</strong> If you already own the Early Access version, you get 1.0.</li>
      <li><strong>Back up before you patch</strong> if you run your own server, and make sure everyone updates to the same version.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2 id="checklist">Launch day checklist</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Back up your world</strong> before the update lands, especially on a private server.</li>
    <li><strong>Re-spend your skill points</strong> at your base before you go anywhere — the tree resets.</li>
    <li><strong>Check your aim assist setting.</strong> New ranged aim assist options are on by default for controllers and off for mouse and keyboard.</li>
    <li><strong>Pick up new spells and try one summon</strong> to see whether a summoner build appeals before committing points.</li>
    <li><strong>Read the patch notes</strong> for final numbers — launched values can differ from the pre-release announcements.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p><strong>When does Enshrouded 1.0 come out?</strong><br />October 15, 2026, on PC (Steam), PlayStation 5 and NVIDIA GeForce Now.</p>
    <p><strong>Is Enshrouded still in Early Access?</strong><br />No. 1.0 is the full release and ends Early Access.</p>
    <p><strong>Is there crossplay at launch?</strong><br />Cross-platform multiplayer is not available at 1.0 launch. Keen Games is working on it without a date.</p>
    <p><strong>Will 1.0 be on Xbox?</strong><br />An Xbox Series X|S version is planned for spring 2027.</p>
    <p><strong>Do my Early Access saves transfer?</strong><br />Yes. They remain usable and are converted to the new save format.</p>
    <p><strong>What is the new biome in Enshrouded 1.0?</strong><br />Cinder's Cradle — a lava-scarred wasteland beneath floating Ancient islands, adding 12 Shroud Roots, two new Hollow Halls and a new enemy faction.</p>
    <p><strong>Which platforms get Enshrouded 1.0?</strong><br />PC (Steam), PlayStation 5 and NVIDIA GeForce Now on October 15, 2026. An Xbox Series X|S version is planned for spring 2027.</p>
    <p><strong>Is the full 1.0 changelog out yet?</strong><br />Not yet. Keen Games has confirmed the headline features and released the 1.0 launch trailer; the full release changelog is due on launch day alongside the Highlights video.</p>
    <p><strong>What time does Enshrouded 1.0 unlock?</strong><br />Keen Games has not given an official time. The PlayStation Store lists the PS5 version for 5pm UTC on October 15, and the Steam update is expected around the same time.</p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0"><strong>What is the new level cap?</strong><br />Player level 50, equipment level 55.</p>
  </div>

